  "changes": [
    "Capture immutable PIN/confirmation before IO; synchronously guard duplicate submit and busy input callbacks.",
    "Align input validation to the existing 6\u201312 ASCII-digit backend contract; invalid inputs/mismatches do not consume a vault attempt.",
    "Run setup/verification and one post-failure lock query on Dispatchers.IO; generic errors never invoke success.",
    "Propagate cancellation and require a current open/foreground gate-session token before success; clear input fields in finally and keep polite feedback."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "ParentSecurity source, keystore alias, encryption, storage and five-attempt/60-second lock policy remain unchanged. This is not PIN reset/recovery or a keystore migration.",
    "Physical runtime tests use synthetic in-memory PinVault only; no stored credential/profile, real PIN UI, keystore or spoken output was accessed/tested.",
    "A synchronous credential write already started in the backend can finish after UI cancellation; no rollback is promised. The cancelled caller cannot subsequently unlock.",
    "Existing backend handling of crypto errors is unchanged; only exceptions escaping vault calls are translated to unavailable feedback.",
    "Setup is allowed only without a configured credential or within the current unlocked parent session; initial save completed in background requires verification on return.",
    "Actual vault/UI/VoiceView, broader device matrix, exact candidate and human gates remain pending."
  ],
